  "notes": "West leads the ♣Q against 5♥. West's club is overtaken by East. As West's lead is almost certainly a singleton, South should win the ♣A.\n\nSouth has no reason not to draw trump. West's 4 spade opening bid indicates an 8 card suit. When West turns up with 3 hearts, it appears his distribution is 8311. South should aim to squeeze East in diamonds and clubs. There are currently 3 losers (1 in spades and 2 in clubs). The count must be rectified to 1 loser without allowing East on lead. If East gains the lead he can play clubs destroying any possible squeeze.\n\nSouth should cash one of dummy's top diamonds, removing West's last non-spade, followed by the ♠A. A spade is exited to West reducing South's loser count to 2. West must continue spades and South discards a club, rectifying the count to 1 loser.\n\nWest plays another spade and South ruffs. South finishes the trumps. On the play of the last heart, a club is discarded from dummy and East is squeezed. A diamond discard makes dummy's diamonds good and a club discard makes South's club good.",
